hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24100","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Idris, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Salamah ibn Sakhr al-Bayadi, he said: I was a man afflicted with women unlike others. He said: When the month of Ramadan entered, I feared, so I did zihar from my wife in the month. He said: While she was serving me one night, something of her became uncovered to me, and I did not remain before I fell upon her. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. So he said: Free a neck. He said: I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I own no neck but my own neck. He said: Then fast two consecutive months. So I said: And did what befell me befall me except from fasting? He said: Then feed sixty poor."
